  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/nh-rsa-data/blob/96bd0a247d4463e2ae692310c0fdd17ec563a46c/rsa_html/III/31/31-117.htm",
  "statuteText": "31:117 Woodstoves. –\n\nTowns may make bylaws providing for the adoption of the model code, promulgated by the state fire marshal pursuant to RSA 153:14, IV, relative to the installation and operation of solid fuel heating appliances and, further, to provide for the inspection of such appliances. A reasonable fee may be charged for such inspection to the owner of the property where such appliance is installed."
